1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:06,701
Har chat app aur har agent asal mein ek
conversation hai: messages ki ek list, jo

2
00:00:06,701 --> 00:00:08,997
time ke saath badhti jaati hai.

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:15,108
Iss lesson mein aap dekhoge ki API kuch
bhi yaad nahi rakhti, history aapke code ki

4
00:00:15,108 --> 00:00:19,367
zimmedari hai, aur badhti
history ka matlab hai badhta bill.

5
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:25,543
Iss lesson ke baad aap explain kar
paoge ki stateless ka matlab kya hai.

6
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:29,683
Multi turn conversation
sahi tareeke se banaoge.

7
00:00:30,033 --> 00:00:34,227
Forgotten reply wala
classic bug pakdoge aur fix karoge.

8
00:00:34,577 --> 00:00:38,598
Aur lambi conversations ko
control mein rakhna seekhoge.

9
00:00:39,898 --> 00:00:42,487
Pehle what: stateless ka matlab kya hai?

10
00:00:42,707 --> 00:00:47,420
Ek call centre socho, jiske paas
customers ka koi record nahi hai.

11
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:53,153
Har baar call karo, toh ek naya agent
phone uthata hai, jo aapke baare mein kuch

12
00:00:53,153 --> 00:00:53,980
nahi jaanta.

13
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,040
Purani problem par help chahiye,
toh poori kahani phirse sunani padegi.

14
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:02,060
API bilkul aise hi kaam karti hai.

15
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,141
Har request akeli hai.

16
00:01:04,491 --> 00:01:06,680
Why aisa design kiya gaya?

17
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,840
Kyunki stateless servers simple hote
hain aur scale karna aasaan hota hai.

18
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:16,031
Koi bhi server kisi bhi
request ko handle kar sakta hai.

19
00:01:16,251 --> 00:01:20,970
Lekin iska matlab hai ki memory
ka kaam aapke code ko karna hai.

20
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:25,755
Ab how: ek conversation
actually kaise chalti hai.

21
00:01:26,105 --> 00:01:29,260
Pehli request mein ek
user message hota hai.

22
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:33,431
API reply karti hai, aur
phir sab bhool jaati hai.

23
00:01:33,651 --> 00:01:38,730
Aapki app user message aur reply,
dono ko ek list mein store karti hai.

24
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:44,602
Doosri request poori list bhejti
hai: pehla question, pehla reply, aur naya

25
00:01:44,602 --> 00:01:45,265
question.

26
00:01:45,615 --> 00:01:48,794
Aur teesri request
paanch messages bhejti hai.

27
00:01:49,014 --> 00:01:52,612
Roles alternate hote
hain, user, assistant, user.

28
00:01:52,832 --> 00:01:56,020
Aur pehla message
hamesha user ka hota hai.

29
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,278
Ab code.

30
00:01:58,498 --> 00:02:02,529
History bas ek Python list
hai, message dictionaries ki.

31
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:08,396
Har question ke liye, pehle usse history
mein append karo, phir poori list messages

32
00:02:08,396 --> 00:02:09,127
mein bhejo.

33
00:02:09,477 --> 00:02:12,188
Phir assistant ka reply bhi append karo.

34
00:02:12,408 --> 00:02:15,571
Yahi woh line hai jo
log aksar bhool jaate hain.

35
00:02:15,921 --> 00:02:21,330
Phir hum print karte hain kitne
messages bheje, aur kitne input tokens lage.

36
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:26,914
Right side dekho: pehle turn mein ek
message gaya, aur paanch input tokens.

37
00:02:27,264 --> 00:02:31,709
Doosre turn mein teen messages
gaye, aur input tokens badh gaye.

38
00:02:31,929 --> 00:02:37,618
Offline fake bhi bata raha hai ki iss
request ke saath kitne purane messages aaye.

39
00:02:37,968 --> 00:02:40,508
Aur teesre turn mein paanch messages.

40
00:02:40,728 --> 00:02:46,470
Har request apne se pehle ka sab kuch
dobara bhejti hai, isliye input tokens har

41
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:47,691
turn badhte hain.

42
00:02:48,991 --> 00:02:51,579
Isko ek table mein dry run karte hain.

43
00:02:51,799 --> 00:02:55,135
Turn one: history mein
sirf ek user message hai.

44
00:02:55,355 --> 00:02:57,583
Ek message gaya, paanch tokens.

45
00:02:57,933 --> 00:03:01,910
Turn two: pehla question,
pehla reply, aur naya question.

46
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:04,648
Teen messages, unhattar tokens.

47
00:03:04,998 --> 00:03:08,342
Turn three: paanch
messages, ek sau chaar tokens.

48
00:03:09,642 --> 00:03:11,259
Ab ek classic bug.

49
00:03:11,479 --> 00:03:15,982
Yeh loop har question append
karta hai, lekin reply kabhi nahi.

50
00:03:16,332 --> 00:03:18,467
Output dekho: user, user.

51
00:03:18,687 --> 00:03:20,820
Koi assistant turn hi nahi hai.

52
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:27,420
API isse accept kar leti hai aur dono
user messages ko ek turn mein merge kar deti

53
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:27,731
hai.

54
00:03:27,951 --> 00:03:32,809
Lekin model ko kabhi pata nahi
chalta ki usne pehle kya bola tha.

55
00:03:33,029 --> 00:03:37,968
Chat app mein yeh aisa lagta hai
jaise assistant ki memory chali gayi ho.

56
00:03:38,188 --> 00:03:41,051
Isliye reply milte hi usse store karo.

57
00:03:42,351 --> 00:03:47,741
Har turn poori history dobara bhejta
hai, toh lambi conversations slow aur mehengi

58
00:03:47,741 --> 00:03:51,751
ho jaati hain, aur aakhir
mein context window bhar jaati hai.

59
00:03:51,971 --> 00:03:54,299
Iske kuch standard solutions hain.

60
00:03:54,649 --> 00:04:00,578
Sabse simple hai sliding window: sirf
latest turns rakho, aur budget cross hone par

61
00:04:00,578 --> 00:04:03,793
sabse purana user aur
assistant pair hata do.

62
00:04:04,013 --> 00:04:06,330
Hamara project yahi karta hai.

63
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:11,891
Doosra option: purane turns ko
model se ek chhoti summary mein badal do.

64
00:04:12,111 --> 00:04:14,204
Yeh Module 6 mein aayega.

65
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:20,297
Teesra: important facts ek database
mein save karo, aur sirf relevant facts wapas

66
00:04:20,297 --> 00:04:20,935
add karo.

67
00:04:21,285 --> 00:04:27,100
Aur prompt caching: conversation ka jo
starting hissa change nahi hua, usse dobara

68
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,653
bhejne par bahut kam bill lagta hai.

69
00:04:29,873 --> 00:04:32,002
Course mein aage yeh use karenge.

70
00:04:33,302 --> 00:04:35,058
Trimming ka ek dry run.

71
00:04:35,278 --> 00:04:41,361
Maan lo history hai user one, assistant
one, user two, assistant two, user three,

72
00:04:41,361 --> 00:04:43,239
aur budget cross ho gaya.

73
00:04:43,459 --> 00:04:47,766
Toh pehla pair hatao: user
one aur assistant one, saath mein.

74
00:04:48,116 --> 00:04:51,719
Ab history hai user two,
assistant two, user three.

75
00:04:51,939 --> 00:04:54,339
Budget ke andar hai, toh bhej do.

76
00:04:54,689 --> 00:05:00,266
Aur yeh galat tareeka hai: sirf user
one hataya, toh history assistant se shuru

77
00:05:00,266 --> 00:05:00,619
hogi.

78
00:05:00,839 --> 00:05:03,011
Roles ka order toot jaata hai.

79
00:05:04,311 --> 00:05:05,770
Interview corner.

80
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:09,840
Messages API stateless
hai, iska kya matlab hai?

81
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:16,059
Answer: server requests ke
beech koi memory nahi rakhta.

82
00:05:16,279 --> 00:05:21,812
Har request mein woh sab hona chahiye
jo model ko chahiye, history ke saath, jo

83
00:05:21,812 --> 00:05:24,963
client store karta
hai aur dobara bhejta hai.

84
00:05:25,183 --> 00:05:29,797
Trap: stateless ka matlab yeh
nahi ki conversation possible nahi.

85
00:05:30,017 --> 00:05:33,646
Conversation chalti hai,
bas state client ke paas hai.

86
00:05:33,996 --> 00:05:39,030
Doosra, scenario based question: ek
lambi chat slow aur mehengi ho rahi hai.

87
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:40,648
Aap kya karoge?

88
00:05:42,998 --> 00:05:46,098
Answer: pehle har turn
ke tokens measure karo.

89
00:05:46,318 --> 00:05:51,928
Phir purane turns ko pairs mein trim
karo, purana context summarise karo, ya facts

90
00:05:51,928 --> 00:05:55,485
ek store mein rakho aur
sirf relevant wale add karo.

91
00:05:55,705 --> 00:05:59,406
Prompt caching unchanged
hisse ki cost kam karti hai.

92
00:05:59,626 --> 00:06:02,999
Trap: bas badi context
window wala model le lo.

93
00:06:03,219 --> 00:06:07,027
Isse problem sirf aage
khisakti hai, aur bill badhta hai.

94
00:06:08,327 --> 00:06:09,584
Practice time.

95
00:06:09,934 --> 00:06:12,713
Pehla: conversation
mein das messages hain.

96
00:06:12,933 --> 00:06:15,710
Agli request kitne messages bhejegi?

97
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:21,798
Doosra: forgetful dot py ko fix karo,
aur batao fix ke baad kaun se roles print

98
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:22,234
honge.

99
00:06:22,584 --> 00:06:26,793
Teesra: ek trim function
likho, jo sabse purane pairs hataye.

100
00:06:27,143 --> 00:06:32,551
Aur scenario: users complain karte hain
ki error ke baad bot sab bhool jaata hai.

101
00:06:32,771 --> 00:06:35,324
Aapka code kya galti kar raha hoga?

102
00:06:42,624 --> 00:06:43,553
Quick check.

103
00:06:43,773 --> 00:06:46,750
Conversation mein
pehle se das messages hain.

104
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:49,747
Agli request kitne messages bhejegi?

105
00:06:55,447 --> 00:06:56,388
Gyaarah.

106
00:06:56,608 --> 00:06:59,517
Saare das purane messages, aur ek naya.

107
00:06:59,737 --> 00:07:03,319
Jab tak aap jaan
boojhkar history trim nahi karte.

108
00:07:04,619 --> 00:07:05,459
Recap.

109
00:07:05,679 --> 00:07:09,650
API stateless hai, aur
history aapka code rakhta hai.

110
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,285
Har turn question aur
reply, dono append karo.

111
00:07:13,635 --> 00:07:17,226
Har turn ke saath input
tokens aur cost badhte hain.

112
00:07:17,576 --> 00:07:20,859
Isliye pairs mein trim
karo, ya summarise karo.

113
00:07:21,209 --> 00:07:26,446
Agle lesson mein aap output ko
control karoge: length limits, streaming, aur

114
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:27,548
structured JSON.
